From d03fd54956602b860c8f357649282d02ad159b90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:20:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2319/2368] media: qcom: camss: log CSID and VFE register
 writes under dynamic debug

Route every register write in the 680 and gen3 CSID and VFE paths through small
inline helpers that emit the block, offset and value through dev_dbg()
before writing. With dynamic debug this costs nothing when disabled and,
when enabled with

  echo 'func vfe_reg_write +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
  echo 'func csid_reg_write +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control

records the complete programming sequence of a stream start in the kernel
log. The sequence is the reference for bringing up the IFE inline
processed path on x1e80100: the same hardware's register programs from
another operating system can be diffed against it, offset by offset.

No functional change.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9b0d00baa00939d768e75ec5dabc610574dfd465)

